.* WRKBNDDIR: the binding directories with their options. The first
.* entry is blank: option 1 on it creates a directory.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=BNDDIR CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=BNDLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=BNDTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=DIRS VARS='OPT BNDDIR BNDLIB BNDTEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKBNDDIR KEYL=KEYS HELP=WRKBNDDH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Binding Directories
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=DIRS VIEWS=2 SCROLL=YES.
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ENTER='RETURN 1'.1=Create
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='RETURN 4'.4=Delete
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPBNDDIR BNDDIR(&BNDLIB./&BNDDIR.)'.5=Display
:LISTACT OPTION=9 ENTER='CMD DSPBNDDIR BNDDIR(&BNDLIB./&BNDDIR.)'.9=Work with binding directory entries
:LISTACT OPTION=13 ENTER='CMD ?CHGOBJD OBJ(&BNDLIB./&BNDDIR.) OBJTYPE(*BNDDIR)'.13=Change description
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=BNDDIR USAGE=OUTPUT.Binding Directory
:LISTCOL VAR=BNDLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:LISTCOL VAR=BNDTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT BNDDIR BNDLIB BNDTEXT'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT BNDDIR BNDLIB'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 5 and 13 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKBNDDH.Work with Binding Directories - Help
:P.The binding directories the name selects. Type 1 on the blank
first line to create one, 4 to delete one, 5 or 9 to see its entries,
13 to change its text.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display, F5 reads the
directories again.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
